<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!-- iOS token-extension entitlements: one keychain group, nothing else.

     An app extension carries its own application-identifier, so by
     default it addresses its own private keychain group and cannot see a
     single item the containing app wrote. Everything the contactless
     path depends on is written by the app and read here - the primed
     identity (CardCore/PrimeStore), the explicitly stored credentials
     (CardCore/CardCredentialStore) and the transport preference
     (CardCore/CardTransportStore). Without this group PrimeStore.read
     returns nil for every card, createToken refuses with primeMissing,
     and no contactless login is possible at all.

     The group is the app's own, and it must stay FIRST in the app's
     array in Config/RefineID-iOS.entitlements: an item added without an
     explicit kSecAttrAccessGroup lands in the first group of the
     writer's entitlement, so reordering that array silently moves every
     write out of this extension's reach.

     Nothing else is granted. The minting and signing path itself was
     proven with no entitlements here, and this adds no capability beyond
     reading what the app already stored on this same device. -->
<dict>
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)fi.refineid.ReFineID</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
